window.manualSearch = {"entries":[{"title":"Getting started","section":"Quick workflow","url":"primeiros-passos.html#quick-workflow","text":"Extract the complete package and have a USB data cable ready. Connect the Cube Baby and wait for the bank to load. Choose the same A/B/C in the app and on the footswitch. Adjust a pedalboard control and listen. You understand connection, editing and listening. Writing the bank is a separate step.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Getting started","url":"primeiros-passos.html","text":"Getting started","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Install and open","url":"primeiros-passos.html#install-and-open","text":"Install and open\r\nExtract the complete package to a folder on your computer and open CubeControl.exe. Keep the package folders next to the executable. The published package does not require the .NET SDK. Simulation is a separate package.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Connect the Cube Baby","url":"primeiros-passos.html#connect-the-cube-baby","text":"Connect the Cube Baby\r\n1. Power on the guitar Cube Baby and connect a USB data cable to the computer.\r\n2. Close other editors using the MIDI port.\r\n3. Open cubeControl and wait for identification and loading of A/B/C and all eight IR slots.\r\n4. If needed, use the connection button and check Device and help for connection details.\r\n\r\nThe editor uses USB-MIDI, not Bluetooth. Cube Baby Bass, AC, Chocolate and Blackbox profiles are not implemented. Manual disconnection pauses automatic reconnection; connecting again resumes it.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Make your first adjustment","url":"primeiros-passos.html#make-your-first-adjustment","text":"Make your first adjustment\r\nSelect the same A/B/C in the app as on the physical pedal. Open a Pedalboard module and adjust a control. Selecting A/B/C in the app chooses the editing destination; it does not operate the footswitch. Read Presets and files before saving.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Customize reading","url":"primeiros-passos.html#customize-reading","text":"Customize reading\r\nTheme, language and zoom are in the ellipsis menu. Documentation works offline without a pedal. Guides follow the app language; PDFs display their own language.\r\n\r\nZoom ranges from 50% to 200% in 10% steps. Use Ctrl +, Ctrl − and Ctrl 0 to increase, decrease and reset to 100%; this does not change Windows DPI. Theme, language and zoom are shared with the simulation edition.\r\n\r\nFor connection issues, see Troubleshooting.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Find help","url":"primeiros-passos.html#find-help","text":"Find help\r\nIn Device and help, cubeControl manual opens the HTML manual in your default browser using the app's current language and theme. It includes full-text search, a chapter index, printing and switching between Portuguese and English. You can also open Assets/Documents/manual/index.html directly, without internet. The browser's theme selection does not change the app's appearance.\r\n\r\nDocumentation Center search matches catalog titles, summaries and keywords, not the full guide text. Every space-separated term must match; case and accents are ignored. If the selected language is unavailable, the app uses Brazilian Portuguese or, failing that, the first available version. Preserved manuals describe their source versions; use the Center’s guides for current app workflows.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Getting started","section":"Navigation and help","url":"primeiros-passos.html#navigation-and-help","text":"Navigation and help\r\nWith the pointer over the main navigation bar, the mouse wheel moves between the five tabs and stops at either end. Outside the bar, scrolling continues to affect the page or control. Use Tab and Shift+Tab for keyboard navigation; Alt alone does not activate navigation cues. Tooltips appear after 1.2 seconds and disappear five seconds after appearing; a new hover can show them again. The documentation window follows the app theme, with zoom applied to its reading content.","keywords":"usb MIDI instalação installation conexão connection busca search zoom idioma language"},{"title":"Pedalboard and effects","section":"Pedalboard and effects","url":"pedaleira.html","text":"Pedalboard and effects","keywords":"tone chorus phaser delay reverb cabinet efeitos effects"},{"title":"Pedalboard and effects","section":"Navigate modules","url":"pedaleira.html#navigate-modules","text":"Navigate modules\r\nThe visual order is Amp → Chorus → Phaser → Delay → Reverb → Cabinet. Click a card to open its editor; its switch performs a separate action. The wheel over the chain navigates between modules.","keywords":"tone chorus phaser delay reverb cabinet efeitos effects"},{"title":"Pedalboard and effects","section":"Understand the controls","url":"pedaleira.html#understand-the-controls","text":"Understand the controls\r\n- Amp Tone is not a general amplifier bypass.\r\n- Chorus and Phaser share a modulation parameter and cannot be active simultaneously.\r\n- Adjustments to a disabled effect may remain local until it is enabled.\r\n- Delay time is a pedal index with no verified conversion to milliseconds. Do not interpret every number as a percentage, Hz or dB.\r\n- Images and commercial names are presentation references, not certification of the contents of a slot.","keywords":"tone chorus phaser delay reverb cabinet efeitos effects"},{"title":"Pedalboard and effects","section":"Choose an amp and cabinet","url":"pedaleira.html#choose-an-amp-and-cabinet","text":"Choose an amp and cabinet\r\nClick the image to open the selector. Apply or double-click confirms; cancel preserves the previous selection. Where a gallery is available, the wheel over the image can also change equipment.\r\n\r\nSee IRs and cabinets or Effect creators for advanced internal adjustments. Changing a picture does not change the sound.","keywords":"tone chorus phaser delay reverb cabinet efeitos effects"},{"title":"Presets, saving and files","section":"Quick workflow","url":"presets.html#quick-workflow","text":"Connect the pedal and load its bank. Export a copy before important changes. Select the target A/B/C and the matching physical preset. Adjust the controls and check the sound. Use Save A/B/C when you want to write the complete bank. The confirmation reports writing and reading the bank; it does not prove retention after power-off.","keywords":"A/B/C JSON salvar save export import desfazer undo"},{"title":"Presets, saving and files","section":"Presets, saving and files","url":"presets.html","text":"Presets, saving and files","keywords":"A/B/C JSON salvar save export import desfazer undo"},{"title":"Presets, saving and files","section":"Edit and listen","url":"presets.html#edit-and-listen","text":"Edit and listen\r\nA/B/C select the preset being edited. Select the matching preset on the physical pedal to hear it. Available adjustments are sent live; saving is still required for persistence.\r\n\r\n Action  Result \r\n ---  --- \r\n Save A/B/C  Writes the complete three-preset bank and checks it by reading back \r\n Export bank  Saves local editing as a JSON file on the computer \r\n Import bank  After confirmation, applies known fields; saving is still required \r\n Read again or reconnect  Loads pedal state; observe replacement and backup messages \r\n Undo  Reverts preset edit history; it does not undo IR or amp writes","keywords":"A/B/C JSON salvar save export import desfazer undo"},{"title":"Presets, saving and files","section":"Keep and recover your work","url":"presets.html#keep-and-recover-your-work","text":"Keep and recover your work\r\nExport the bank before major changes. Reading back does not prove retention after power-off. Use the correct files: bank JSON for A/B/C, WAV for IR, BIN for amp and a dedicated JSON format for each effect creator.\r\n\r\nSee Backups and recovery and Pedalboard.","keywords":"A/B/C JSON salvar save export import desfazer undo"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Quick workflow","url":"irs.html#quick-workflow","text":"Have a compatible impulse-response WAV and a backup of the slot you intend to replace. Open Manage IRs and select a file in the individual tab. With the pedal connected, check the preview state and listen. End the preview to restore, or use the write action and check its destination. Previewing and replacing a slot have different outcomes; check the message before continuing.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"IRs, cabinets and associations","url":"irs.html","text":"IRs, cabinets and associations","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Choose a cabinet","url":"irs.html#choose-a-cabinet","text":"Choose a cabinet\r\nThe pedal has eight IR slots. Their contents may have been replaced: a slot number does not identify a cabinet. The included library works offline.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Shared library","url":"irs.html#shared-library","text":"Shared library\r\nManage IRs has Individual analysis and preview and IR packs tabs sharing the same library, search and selection. The individual tab opens initially; the selected tab is retained during the session. In Packs, selecting a file only makes it available for slot assembly. Switching tabs does not apply IRs or discard the draft; an active preview remains on the pedal. Return to the individual tab to end it.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Import and try an IR","url":"irs.html#import-and-try-an-ir","text":"Import and try an IR\r\nChoose an impulse-response WAV in the interface and check the reported compatibility. An IR WAV is neither an amp file nor a Backing Tracks song. IR preview changes pedal RAM without replacing any of the eight stored slots. Choosing an external WAV or selecting an IR in the individual library starts preview automatically when the pedal is connected and the session is not blocked; without a connection, it only prepares the local file. The previous state remains in memory for this app session; use End preview before closing.\r\n\r\nImporting to a slot and writing are device operations. Export or preserve the backup of the previous contents before replacement. Read the messages and the destination slot in the confirmation.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Audition with recorded guitar","url":"irs.html#audition-with-recorded-guitar","text":"Audition with recorded guitar\r\nSelect one of the five guitar recordings and choose the pedal’s USB audio output. An operational MIDI connection is required, but loading an IR is optional. Without an IR preview you hear the current preset. Audition follows changes applied to the effect chain, including Amp Creator previews; edits that remain only on the computer do not affect the sound. An interrupted IR preview must be confirmed or restored before starting. The computer plays the raw WAV; the pedal processes it with its current effects. Outputs come from Windows: choosing another output does not apply the IR in software. Volume starts at 30% and looping is enabled.\r\n\r\nChanging the IR pauses and mutes audition during transfer; playback resumes at the same position only after confirmation. Pause keeps the position; Stop returns to the beginning. Changing the recording during playback restarts with the new recording. Playback continues when navigating to the pedalboard or Amp Creator, with compact pause and stop controls. Ending IR preview pauses during restoration and resumes the restored preset after confirmation. Changing output, disconnecting or closing the app stops playback. Backing Tracks, YouTube previews and IR audition do not play simultaneously.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Build and apply packs","url":"irs.html#build-and-apply-packs","text":"Build and apply packs\r\nThe catalog includes 34 predefined packs, grouped by brand, style and guitar, with eight slots and an initial distance of 80%. Descriptions suggest uses; they do not simulate guitar models or imply listening validation. Personal packs appear under My packs.\r\n\r\nIn IR packs, choose any pack and edit it directly. The first change to a predefined pack creates an independent draft and shows the yellow Creating pack notice; the original stays intact. Remove all eight IRs to start empty. Drag a library file onto the destination card. Dragging between cards swaps their IRs and distances. The trash icon appears on hover or keyboard focus; Delete also removes an IR. The context menu provides keyboard alternatives. Empty slots preserve the pedal's current contents. Building and searching do not start a preview or write to the device.\r\n\r\nAdjust Volume directly with each card’s knob, from 0 to 99% (distance in the protocol). Its value appears in the tooltip and is stored when saving the pack. Click Apply to send populated slots: only an action confirmation appears, with OK or Exit. The app compares destinations, keeps a backup and skips identical contents. Empty slots remain unchanged; fix or remove missing references before applying.\r\n\r\nThe Apply and Restore original IRs actions appear below the grid. Save pack asks for a name and description in a popup and stores your draft for reuse; saving is optional before applying. Saving a draft based on a predefined pack creates a personal pack; saving changes to a personal pack updates it. Discarding restores the source pack. When switching a changed pack, choose Save, Discard, or Cancel.\r\n\r\nExport creates a .cubeirpack.zip containing the WAVs, which can be imported on another computer. Import opens a draft for review without automatically saving or applying it. Imported WAVs are stored in user data and also appear in the individual library. Older .cubeirpack.json files remain supported but require their referenced WAVs. Missing references are shown on cards and cannot be selected for application.\r\n\r\nBinary BFI/BFIN packs are available through the separate Restore original IRs action when original resources are available. See Backups and recovery.\r\n\r\nThe BFIN pack identified by content uses the following references, with matching names, images and descriptions. Off is separate from the eight IRs; it occupies the first row in the source table, before Line 6 Vetta.\r\n\r\n IR slot  BFIN reference  Cab type \r\n---------\r\n 1  Line 6 Vetta  2×12 \r\n 2  Marshall 1960AV  4×12 \r\n 3  Marshall 1960A T75 LA610  4×12 \r\n 4  VHT Deliverance  2×12 \r\n 5  Soldano  2×12 \r\n 6  Peavey 5150 + Mesa Oversized  4×12 \r\n 7  JSX KT77 + Mesa Stiletto AKG C1000  4×12 \r\n 8  Diezel V30 SM57 (Soldano HR PowerAmp)  4×12 \r\n\r\nReferences follow recognized content even when moved to another slot. Custom names and images remain available.\r\n\r\n Limits and partial application\r\nIndividual WAVs and WAVs in a portable pack are limited to 32 MiB per file. The pack validates all WAV hashes and formats before copying them to the imported library; changed or invalid files are rejected. Importing a ZIP can already copy WAVs to user data before you save the draft.\r\n\r\nApplying a pack writes one slot at a time. If it fails, the message lists completed slots; it does not automatically undo slots already written. Check the result before retrying. Automatic copies of previous contents remain only in session memory; export backups you need to keep.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Random cabinet IR","url":"irs.html#random-cabinet-ir","text":"Random cabinet IR\r\nIn the effect chain, under Cabinet, Randomize and apply chooses from the entire library, including imports and ignoring search filters, with an integer volume from 66% to 85% (the protocol calls this parameter distance). The destination is the current preset cabinet, not the separately selected slot on the IR page. It writes directly without another confirmation and applies in RAM for immediate use; it does not save the preset or change the IR section on/off state. Repeats are possible.\r\n\r\nA working connection, loaded bank, valid slot and available library are required. The file is validated before writing. If writing succeeds but immediate application fails, the message distinguishes the two: the slot has already been replaced. Previous contents are retained only in session memory.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Associate with an amp","url":"irs.html#associate-with-an-amp","text":"Associate with an amp\r\nAssociate cabinet applies the configured amp association to the edited preset. Associations and the automatic-association option remain in the current session only; reopening starts with automatic association disabled and requires configuring associations again. Saving associations does not send commands to the pedal. When enabled, it attempts to apply the association to the current amp and subsequent choices. Without a valid association, the cabinet is preserved.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Identity and pictures","url":"irs.html#identity-and-pictures","text":"Identity and pictures\r\nManufacturer names and photos help selection but do not prove that an IR exactly reproduces that equipment. Visual customization does not change audio.\r\n\r\nSee Backups and recovery.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"IRs, cabinets and associations","section":"Overdriven.fr collections","url":"irs.html#overdrivenfr-collections","text":"Overdriven.fr collections\r\n\r\nThe Overdriven.fr library contains 13 collections and 682 IRs. Search matches every typed term, case-insensitively, against file paths, names and metadata. Clear the text to restore the full library. There are no separate collection, microphone or distance selectors. Searching does not send audio to the pedal; selecting an IR in the individual library can start preview.\r\n\r\nFiles with metadata follow brand → speaker configuration → model and speaker → capture. Overdriven.fr identifies the source, not a cabinet brand. Files without metadata follow their folders; imported files appear under Imported IRs. Expanding one brand collapses the others. Selection details show original format, source, identification, evidence, position, variants and filename. Microphone models\r\nmarked “inspired by” come from the provider documentation. Undocumented codes\r\nare preserved without assumed equivalents.\r\n\r\nIn the provider's visual reference, P00 is the dust cap center, P05 is on the\r\ncap, P09 near its edge, P10 at its edge, P20 on the cone and P30 near the outer\r\nedge. Other codes, such as P12 and P25, have no exact documented location in\r\nthat image. The original photo is not bundled with the app.\r\n\r\nFilename distances are approximate millimeters. They describe the capture\r\nand do not change the app's 0–99 Distance control. Suffixes such as LC45,\r\nEQ, P0, CUT1 and UA610 identify variants, without triggering processing in the\r\napp. SP1-PREVIEW marks preview files, each identified by its own microphone and\r\noriginal name.\r\n\r\nAll files are mono at 44.1 kHz: 82 GOV IRs are PCM 16-bit/50 ms (their readme\r\nstates float 32-bit); the rest are PCM 24-bit/100 ms. The app converts to 48 kHz\r\nand retains 512 samples, approximately 10.7 ms, without gain normalization.\r\nIt applies no automatic cuts, EQ, gain or phase correction. The provider's\r\nfilter and adjustment recommendations are listening suggestions.","keywords":"IR WAV cabinet gabinete associação association biblioteca library pré-escuta audition guitarra guitar pack partial parcial"},{"title":"Amp creator","section":"Quick workflow","url":"criador-amps.html#quick-workflow","text":"Have a base amp or a valid 4096-byte BIN. Preserve the old content before writing. Choose the source and check whether preview is active. Adjust gradually and compare with the reference. Export BIN to keep a local copy; use Save to pedal only to replace the confirmed slot. The BIN preserves your local edit. After writing, switch amps on the pedal and back to reload the slot.","keywords":"amp BIN RAM gain EQ flash"},{"title":"Amp creator","section":"Amp creator","url":"criador-amps.html","text":"Amp creator","keywords":"amp BIN RAM gain EQ flash"},{"title":"Amp creator","section":"Prepare an edit","url":"criador-amps.html#prepare-an-edit","text":"Prepare an edit\r\nChoose a base amp or import a valid 4096-byte BIN. This format is not a cabinet WAV, preset JSON or NAM model. Offline import prepares a local edit.","keywords":"amp BIN RAM gain EQ flash"},{"title":"Amp creator","section":"Adjust and listen","url":"criador-amps.html#adjust-and-listen","text":"Adjust and listen\r\nSelecting the source in the interface attempts to start preview when the pedal is available. Adjustments trigger automatic preview. Preview changes shared RAM for the active amp: selecting a source does not prove which amp is physically active. Changing the amp on the pedal may reload its RAM.\r\n\r\nCreator gain and volume change internal tables; they differ from the preset GAIN and VOLUME controls. Classic/Modern EQ are presentation choices. Adjust gradually within the displayed limits.","keywords":"amp BIN RAM gain EQ flash"},{"title":"Amp creator","section":"Precise editing and response profiles","url":"criador-amps.html#precise-editing-and-response-profiles","text":"Precise editing and response profiles\r\nClick a value or press Enter to type it; Enter confirms and Escape or leaving the field discards it. Restore band recovers that EQ's parameters and coefficients. The value marker indicates a difference from the loaded reference, not from factory contents.\r\n\r\nResponse provides two capacitor panels with profile and intensity. Original and zero intensity preserve the reference. Profiles are listening proposals, not a calibrated electrical simulation. Restore original affects only the chosen panel. Importing, reading or loading sets a new reference without trying to infer profiles from the imported sound.\r\n\r\nDouble-click a knob or fader to restore the loaded reference; Backspace with the control focused does the same. EQ resets the entire band; Response resets the original profile and intensity.","keywords":"amp BIN RAM gain EQ flash"},{"title":"Amp creator","section":"Export, restore and write","url":"criador-amps.html#export-restore-and-write","text":"Export, restore and write\r\n- Export BIN saves your edit on the computer.\r\n- Restore attempts to return the RAM captured at the start of preview.\r\n- Save to pedal replaces the sector for the slot shown in the confirmation. This is persistent and cannot be undone through preset history.\r\n\r\nKeep backups and read Recovery. In simulation, device amp reading, preview and writing are disabled; local files remain available.\r\n\r\nAfter a successful write, select another amp on the pedal and return to reload the slot. Byte read-back confirmation does not prove retention after power-off or physical sound reloading.","keywords":"amp BIN RAM gain EQ flash"},{"title":"Using effect creators","section":"Using effect creators","url":"criadores-efeitos.html","text":"Using effect creators","keywords":"criador creator RAM gráfico graph preview prévia"},{"title":"Using effect creators","section":"Open and adjust","url":"criadores-efeitos.html#open-and-adjust","text":"Open and adjust\r\nOn the Pedalboard, open the effect’s Advanced options. Opening already attempts to prepare and start preview; returning to simple editing neither ends it nor restores parameters. Use the effect’s restore action to end preview and recover the previous state. Manipulate the graph contours directly. The selected element displays its numeric details. Keyboard focus allows adjustment without dragging.\r\n\r\nDrawings are illustrative, not acoustic-response measurements. Normal pedal controls remain separate from creators.","keywords":"criador creator RAM gráfico graph preview prévia"},{"title":"Using effect creators","section":"Select and type a parameter","url":"criadores-efeitos.html#select-and-type-a-parameter","text":"Select and type a parameter\r\nThe panel provides a parameter list and slider as alternatives to graph handles. Click the value or press Enter with a handle selected to type. Enter confirms and Escape cancels; leaving the field attempts to apply a valid value. Invalid or out-of-range values are not sent. The panel sits beside the graph when space allows and above it at narrower widths.","keywords":"criador creator RAM gráfico graph preview prévia"},{"title":"Using effect creators","section":"Preview and persistence","url":"criadores-efeitos.html#preview-and-persistence","text":"Preview and persistence\r\nWhen starting a new preview, the app checks the firmware and requires PRESET mode on the pedal. It reads the physical preset and selects the matching A/B/C in the interface. Preparation may send live adjustments to enable the section and give the effect an audible level before capturing its reference; Read active effect is therefore not a read-only operation. These adjustments may leave unsaved bank changes. The app cannot remotely change the physical pedal mode. Other operations may be blocked during preview to prevent conflicts.\r\n\r\nChorus, phaser, delay and reverb creators modify RAM: they do not write their adjustments to flash or guarantee persistence after power-off. Export saves a local file; import prepares an edit, and Apply settings sends it to an active preview.","keywords":"criador creator RAM gráfico graph preview prévia"},{"title":"Using effect creators","section":"Specific guides","url":"criadores-efeitos.html#specific-guides","text":"Specific guides\r\n- Chorus\r\n- Phaser\r\n- Delay\r\n- Reverb\r\n- Backups and recovery","keywords":"criador creator RAM gráfico graph preview prévia"},{"title":"Chorus creator","section":"Chorus creator","url":"criador-chorus.html","text":"Chorus creator","keywords":"chorus RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Chorus creator","section":"Prepare preview","url":"criador-chorus.html#prepare-preview","text":"Prepare preview\r\nSelect PRESET mode and the desired A/B/C physically on the pedal. On the Pedalboard, open the effect’s Advanced options: this already attempts to prepare and start preview. The app selects the detected physical preset in the interface. Preparation selects chorus and enables the delay/modulation section when needed. This preparation may change live parameters without saving the bank. An incompatible profile or context prevents preview; see Using effect creators.","keywords":"chorus RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Chorus creator","section":"Controls","url":"criador-chorus.html#controls","text":"Controls\r\nDepth, estimated speed, processed-branch mix, feedback, waveform and delayed/combined branch gains. Processed-branch mix is not a wet percentage.","keywords":"chorus RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Chorus creator","section":"Files and restoration","url":"criador-chorus.html#files-and-restoration","text":"Files and restoration\r\nImport .chorus.json prepares local settings; Apply settings sends them to an active preview. Export does not write to the pedal. There is no persistent flash write or preview for this effect on the simulated device.\r\n\r\nRestore chorus, normal disconnection, reading again and normal closing attempt to return the original parameters. Lost connection or a context change stops writes; an attempted restoration is not confirmation of success.\r\n\r\nThe recovery snapshot exists only in memory for this app session. If the connection is lost, reconnect the same device and use Restore chorus, subject to the context checks performed by the app. Closing or restarting the app discards this snapshot; old recovery files are not loaded automatically. Export any adjustments you want to keep.\r\n\r\nSee Effect creators and Backups and recovery.","keywords":"chorus RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Phaser creator","section":"Phaser creator","url":"criador-phaser.html","text":"Phaser creator","keywords":"phaser RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Phaser creator","section":"Prepare preview","url":"criador-phaser.html#prepare-preview","text":"Prepare preview\r\nSelect PRESET mode and the desired A/B/C physically on the pedal. On the Pedalboard, open the effect’s Advanced options: this already attempts to prepare and start preview. The app selects the detected physical preset in the interface. Preparation selects phaser and enables the delay/modulation section when needed. This preparation may change live parameters without saving the bank. An incompatible profile or context prevents preview; see Using effect creators.","keywords":"phaser RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Phaser creator","section":"Controls","url":"criador-phaser.html#controls","text":"Controls\r\nEstimated speed and frequency endpoints, level and section count. The lower endpoint must not exceed the upper one. Estimated values are not acoustic measurements.","keywords":"phaser RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Phaser creator","section":"Files and restoration","url":"criador-phaser.html#files-and-restoration","text":"Files and restoration\r\nImport .phaser.json prepares local settings; Apply settings sends them to an active preview. Export does not write to the pedal. There is no persistent flash write or preview for this effect on the simulated device.\r\n\r\nRestore phaser, normal disconnection, reading again and normal closing attempt to return the original parameters. Lost connection or a context change stops writes; an attempted restoration is not confirmation of success.\r\n\r\nThe recovery snapshot exists only in memory for this app session. If the connection is lost, reconnect the same device and use Restore phaser, subject to the context checks performed by the app. Closing or restarting the app discards this snapshot; old recovery files are not loaded automatically. Export any adjustments you want to keep.\r\n\r\nSee Effect creators and Backups and recovery.","keywords":"phaser RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Delay creator","section":"Delay creator","url":"criador-delay.html","text":"Delay creator","keywords":"delay RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Delay creator","section":"Prepare preview","url":"criador-delay.html#prepare-preview","text":"Prepare preview\r\nSelect PRESET mode and the desired A/B/C physically on the pedal. On the Pedalboard, open the effect’s Advanced options: this already attempts to prepare and start preview. The app selects the detected physical preset in the interface. Preparation enables the delay/modulation section and raises the mix if it is zero; disabling chorus/phaser is not required. This preparation may change live parameters without saving the bank. An incompatible profile or context prevents preview; see Using effect creators.","keywords":"delay RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Delay creator","section":"Controls","url":"criador-delay.html#controls","text":"Controls\r\nThe graph offers temporal modulation depth and speed, time in internal samples and fine feedback/mix resolution. Depth and speed are percentages of the original: zero depth removes oscillation; zero speed freezes its phase. Effective speed depends on time. Internal mix 50 keeps dry and echo signals at full level; it is not a complementary wet/dry sum. Millisecond equivalence has not been verified by audio measurement.","keywords":"delay RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Delay creator","section":"Files and restoration","url":"criador-delay.html#files-and-restoration","text":"Files and restoration\r\nImport .delay.json prepares local settings; Apply settings sends them to an active preview. Export does not write to the pedal. There is no persistent flash write or preview for this effect on the simulated device.\r\n\r\nRestore delay, normal disconnection, reading again and normal closing attempt to return the original parameters. Lost connection or a context change stops writes; an attempted restoration is not confirmation of success.\r\n\r\nThe recovery snapshot exists only in memory for this app session. If the connection is lost, reconnect the same device and use Restore delay, subject to the context checks performed by the app. Closing or restarting the app discards this snapshot; old recovery files are not loaded automatically. Export any adjustments you want to keep.\r\n\r\nSee Effect creators and Backups and recovery.","keywords":"delay RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Reverb creator","section":"Reverb creator","url":"criador-reverb.html","text":"Reverb creator","keywords":"reverb RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Reverb creator","section":"Prepare preview","url":"criador-reverb.html#prepare-preview","text":"Prepare preview\r\nSelect PRESET mode and the desired A/B/C physically on the pedal. On the Pedalboard, open the effect’s Advanced options: this already attempts to prepare and start preview. The app selects the detected physical preset in the interface. Preparation enables the reverb/cabinet section and raises reverb if it is zero; disabling modulation is not required. This preparation may change live parameters without saving the bank. An incompatible profile or context prevents preview; see Using effect creators.","keywords":"reverb RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Reverb creator","section":"Controls","url":"criador-reverb.html#controls","text":"Controls\r\nDry signal, reverberated signal, feedback, line return and damping. Adjust gradually within the editor ranges.","keywords":"reverb RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Reverb creator","section":"Files and restoration","url":"criador-reverb.html#files-and-restoration","text":"Files and restoration\r\nImport .reverb.json prepares local settings; Apply settings sends them to an active preview. Export does not write to the pedal. There is no persistent flash write or preview for this effect on the simulated device.\r\n\r\nRestore reverb, normal disconnection, reading again and normal closing attempt to return the original parameters. Lost connection or a context change stops writes; an attempted restoration is not confirmation of success.\r\n\r\nThe recovery snapshot exists only in memory for this app session. If the connection is lost, reconnect the same device and use Restore reverb, subject to the context checks performed by the app. Closing or restarting the app discards this snapshot; old recovery files are not loaded automatically. Export any adjustments you want to keep.\r\n\r\nSee Effect creators and Backups and recovery.","keywords":"reverb RAM prévia preview restaurar restore"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Quick workflow","url":"backing-tracks.html#quick-workflow","text":"Have an MP3/WAV and a Windows audio output. Recording also requires an audio input. Add a track and choose the output. Play it and use A/B to practise a section. To record, configure the input, arm a track with R and use REC. You can listen and keep takes. The playlist references audio files; keep those files available.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Backing Tracks","url":"backing-tracks.html","text":"Backing Tracks","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Prepare your guitar","url":"backing-tracks.html#prepare-your-guitar","text":"Prepare your guitar\r\n\r\nUse Import to create MP3/WAV tracks and New track, in Options, for an empty track. In Prepare guitar, select the track, input device and mono/stereo channels. Arm recording prepares REC. Monitor input starts off when opening a project; input meters work even without listening. Input clipping means you should lower the device's input level.\r\n\r\nChoose headphone/speaker output in the same panel. S/M/R/I mean Solo, Mute, Arm recording and Monitor input. Headers and mixer share their state. One capture device is used at a time, with channels assigned to tracks.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Record and review takes","url":"backing-tracks.html#record-and-review-takes","text":"Record and review takes\r\n\r\nRecord starts at the cursor after a count-in of zero, one or two bars, even with metronome off for the recording itself. With A/B Loop enabled, it records one pass from A to B.\r\n\r\nFinish take or Stop closes the recording, pauses and returns to its start. Select a clip to choose its active take, edit its name and use Listen to take, Previous or Next. Recording again preserves earlier alternatives in the overlapping region and audio outside it.\r\n\r\nGain, pan, mute and solo remain adjustable during REC. Input, channels, arming, monitoring and structural editing stay locked until finalization. Recorded files contain the signal before gain and pan; accompaniment and metronome are not automatically captured.\r\n\r\nAfter an interruption, restore the project and use Recover interrupted take to attempt a usable copy of the selected track's latest interrupted recording. The original remains intact. Ignore interrupted take removes only the reference and supports Undo; it does not delete audio. Physical accuracy depends on devices; latency compensation is under Audio options.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Projects and recovery","url":"backing-tracks.html#projects-and-recovery","text":"Projects and recovery\r\n\r\nNew, Open, Save, Save as and Recent projects manage .cubeproject files. Keep the file together with its Media folder. Audio, recordings and alternate takes are copied there when saving. Moving the complete folder preserves references; Save as in another folder creates new copies. Originals are not deleted.\r\n\r\nThe indicator distinguishes temporary projects, unsaved changes and saved projects. Automatic recovery keeps recent changes without replacing manual saves. After interruption, choose Restore or Discard. Closing or switching a changed project offers Save, Discard or Cancel.\r\n\r\nOptions lets you select older sessions for import. Import legacy session, in the project toolbar overflow, can also open an older playlist. Save the result as a project; previous data is preserved. For missing media, use Locate clip audio or Locate track audio before saving again.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Timeline and editing","url":"backing-tracks.html#timeline-and-editing","text":"Timeline and editing\r\n\r\nDrag clips to move them and edges to trim. Upper handles adjust fades; numerical fields use seconds. Crossfade is available for two overlapping clips on the same track. Edits do not modify original audio.\r\n\r\nSnap follows the musical division; Alt bypasses alignment while dragging. Cut splits selected clips at the cursor, or clips on the selected track. Undo/Redo includes takes, fades and mixing.\r\n\r\nBPM defines the grid without stretching audio. Apply suggested BPM confirms analysis. Speed changes playback; Pitch transposes from −6 to +6 semitones. Completing analysis preserves zoom.\r\n\r\nSet A/B using the ruler menu and drag its markers. Loop repeats the region during playback. The metronome menu provides meter, accent, sound and first-beat settings.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Mixer and library","url":"backing-tracks.html#mixer-and-library","text":"Mixer and library\r\n\r\nMixer opens real track channels and Master; drag its divider to resize. Library opens Local files and YouTube. Panels start collapsed on a new installation and remember your preference. In small windows, preparation/library alternate with the timeline; transport stays accessible. Additional commands appear in toolbar overflow menus.\r\n\r\nFor local audio, Add folder indexes MP3/WAV. Search combines with All, Loops, One Shots and Vocals; assign categories through the file menu. Preview toggles to Stop preview. The session pauses without automatically resuming. Insert adds a clip at the cursor; dragging chooses track and position.\r\n\r\nOn YouTube, search, preview up to 30 seconds and download to a chosen folder. Add to project creates a track after downloading. These features require internet; use content you own or are authorized to use. Hover preview is optional and remembered.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Backing Tracks","section":"Export and shortcuts","url":"backing-tracks.html#export-and-shortcuts","text":"Export and shortcuts\r\n\r\nExport offers mix/selected track and full session/A/B. Applying speed and pitch is enabled by default. Mixdown includes gains, pan, mute, solo and Master, excluding metronome and live input. Isolated-track export ignores mute/solo and retains gain, pan and Master. Output is 48 kHz stereo PCM16 WAV. Source audio is protected from overwrite.\r\n\r\nCtrl+S saves; Ctrl+O opens; Ctrl+N creates a project. Space plays/pauses; Home returns to the start or A; L toggles loop. Ctrl+Z/Ctrl+Y undo/redo. In the timeline, Ctrl+C/Ctrl+V copy/paste, Ctrl+D duplicates and Delete removes clips. Alt+arrows moves by 0.01 s; Alt+Shift+arrows by 0.1 s. Shift+F10 opens clip actions. F6 switches navigation/content.","keywords":"MP3 WAV YouTube BPM loop Bluetooth áudio audio"},{"title":"Simulation","section":"Simulation","url":"simulacao.html","text":"Simulation","keywords":"simulação simulation offline virtual"},{"title":"Simulation","section":"Open simulation","url":"simulacao.html#open-simulation","text":"Open simulation\r\nUse the separate simulation package. The window title and Cube Baby SIMULADO port identify it. The normal edition cannot switch to simulation while running.","keywords":"simulação simulation offline virtual"},{"title":"Simulation","section":"What to try","url":"simulacao.html#what-to-try","text":"What to try\r\nYou can edit, save and reload A/B/C and perform IR operations in virtual memory. Disconnecting and reconnecting preserves memory within the same process; closing the app resets the virtual pedal. Recovery snapshots are also temporary and are not resumed after restart. Export banks you want to keep.","keywords":"simulação simulation offline virtual"},{"title":"Simulation","section":"Limitations","url":"simulacao.html#limitations","text":"Limitations\r\nSimulation does not generate DSP audio or validate physical USB, real erasure or retention without power. IR slots start empty. Device amp preview/writing and effect-creator previews are unavailable. Local amp import/export remain available. Backing Tracks uses real Windows audio.","keywords":"simulação simulation offline virtual"},{"title":"Simulation","section":"Local data","url":"simulacao.html#local-data","text":"Local data\r\nThe editor uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CubeControl-Simulation. Theme, language and zoom are shared in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CubeControl.\r\n\r\nSee Getting started.","keywords":"simulação simulation offline virtual"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Backups and recovery","url":"recuperacao.html","text":"Backups and recovery","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Keep your edits","url":"recuperacao.html#keep-your-edits","text":"Keep your edits\r\nExport the A/B/C bank, BIN models and creator files as appropriate. Keep original WAVs and songs separately. Exporting does not write to the pedal.","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Interrupted preview","url":"recuperacao.html#interrupted-preview","text":"Interrupted preview\r\nThe previous state is held in memory during the current app session. If the connection is lost, reconnect the same device and use the feature's restore action, subject to profile and context checks. Restarting the app discards the snapshots; a preview from a previous session is not recovered automatically. Normal closing attempts to restore effect, amp and IR previews and reports failures before offering to close anyway.","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Preserve files","url":"recuperacao.html#preserve-files","text":"Preserve files\r\nAutomatic bank, IR and amp copies retained by the editor are temporary and held in memory. To keep data between sessions, explicitly export it to your chosen location. Preferences and images reside in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CubeControl; simulation editor data uses CubeControl-Simulation. Old recovery files are not loaded automatically.","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Factory recovery","url":"recuperacao.html#factory-recovery","text":"Factory recovery\r\nFactory recovery and slot replacement are different from undo. Read the confirmation, check the destination and preserve edits before proceeding. Preset history cannot undo IR or amp sector writes.\r\n\r\nFactory preset restoration looks for %USERPROFILE%\\Downloads\\CubeSuite\\CubeSuite.exe and bin\\BFI.bin in that installation. The app validates specific versions by size/hash; missing or unrecognized files make this feature unavailable. This flow has no source-location picker. Restore original IRs checks BFI/BFIN packs separately in the same bin folder. These external resources are not bundled with cubeControl; FactoryAmps.bin does not replace them.","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Reinstall or update firmware","url":"recuperacao.html#reinstall-or-update-firmware","text":"Reinstall or update firmware\r\nIn Device and help, disconnect the editor’s MIDI session before installing. Select a listed .up or choose a file; refreshing the list does not write to the pedal. The app validates the format, but this does not establish that the variant is suitable for your device. Installation is unavailable in the simulation edition.\r\n\r\nExport any data you want to keep: presets and IRs may be replaced. Close flash_loader and enter flash mode by powering on the pedal connected to the PC while holding the third footswitch, as stated in the app’s confirmation. After confirmation, Windows requests administrator permission. Do not power off or disconnect during writing. Progress and errors appear in the editor; this is different from restoring only presets or IRs. If writing is interrupted, follow the error message before retrying; automatic restoration of the previous firmware is not guaranteed.","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Backups and recovery","section":"Confirm the result","url":"recuperacao.html#confirm-the-result","text":"Confirm the result\r\nWatch for read-back confirmation. Lost connection or incompatible context can prevent restoration. Model identification is not a unique serial number; use the same pedal and the correct context.\r\n\r\nSee Troubleshooting.","keywords":"backup restaurar restore fábrica factory RAM flash recovery firmware atualização update"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"Troubleshooting","url":"problemas.html","text":"Troubleshooting","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"The pedal does not connect","url":"problemas.html#the-pedal-does-not-connect","text":"The pedal does not connect\r\nCheck power and a USB data cable. Close other MIDI editors and try connecting again. Check connection details in Device and help. Bluetooth does not replace USB-MIDI.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"I change a preset but cannot hear it","url":"problemas.html#i-change-a-preset-but-cannot-hear-it","text":"I change a preset but cannot hear it\r\nCheck that A/B/C in the app matches the pedal. Check switches and physical sections. Selecting a preset in the app does not operate the footswitch. Resolve any pending recovery before starting another preview.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"Settings disappeared after power-off","url":"problemas.html#settings-disappeared-after-power-off","text":"Settings disappeared after power-off\r\nLive adjustments are not persistent writes. Save the bank for A/B/C. Chorus/phaser/delay/reverb creators work only in RAM; export their files to keep the edits.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"A track will not play","url":"problemas.html#a-track-will-not-play","text":"A track will not play\r\nCheck that its MP3/WAV still exists at the original path and that the audio output is available. Check volume and mute. YouTube search requires a network; local playback does not.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"REC unavailable or recording has no audio","url":"problemas.html#rec-unavailable-or-recording-has-no-audio","text":"REC unavailable or recording has no audio\r\nSelect the input and channels in Prepare guitar and arm the track. Input metering works with monitoring off. REC does not automatically capture accompaniment or metronome. Finish take or Stop finalizes and returns to the take start; with A/B Loop enabled, recording ends at B. After interruption, restore the project and use Recover interrupted take. See Record.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"The exported WAV sounds different from the player","url":"problemas.html#the-exported-wav-sounds-different-from-the-player","text":"The exported WAV sounds different from the player\r\nMix export includes gain, pan, mute, solo and Master. Applying speed and pitch is enabled by default; A/B can define the range with looping off. Isolated-track export ignores mute/solo. See Export.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"A document will not open","url":"problemas.html#a-document-will-not-open","text":"A document will not open\r\nGuides are included in the package. If files are missing, extract the complete package again. PDFs require an associated Windows reader. Web links require a browser and connection.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Troubleshooting","section":"Before requesting support","url":"problemas.html#before-requesting-support","text":"Before requesting support\r\nRecord the app version, displayed message and steps that reproduce the issue. Keep backups and review paths or other personal data before sharing logs.","keywords":"erro error conexão connection som sound suporte support"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Privacy","url":"privacidade.html","text":"Privacy\r\n\r\nUpdated: October 19, 2026. Scope: cubeControl 1.1.0 for Windows, including amp creator and Backing Tracks.\r\n\r\nApplication controller: Luiz Paulo Martins Ferreira. Privacy contact: lzpmartins@gmail.com.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Local operation","url":"privacidade.html#local-operation","text":"Local operation\r\nThe HTML manual works offline and searches its content inside the browser without sending queries. When supported, it saves only the theme preference in the cube-manual-theme local-storage key. Clearing browser data removes this preference. External and email links open only when selected by the user.\r\n\r\nPedal editing uses USB-MIDI. No account, registration, advertising, developer analytics or automatic upload to developer servers is required. Included IRs and local audio playback work offline. Windows audio output may use Bluetooth; the Bluetooth button opens Windows settings.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Information and purposes","url":"privacidade.html#information-and-purposes","text":"Information and purposes\r\nThe app uses MIDI port names and pedal identification to connect; presets, effects, amp data and IRs to edit, preview and restore; language, appearance, zoom and visual preferences to customize the interface; chosen WAVs, images, backups and BIN files for import/export and recovery; MP3/WAV paths, list order, output, volume and mute to organize the list and control playback during the current session. Loop points, position, speed and waveforms support practice and export. Backup dates and integrity checks support recovery. Connection/error messages support diagnosis.\r\n\r\nNames, paths and selected content may contain personal information. Avoid unnecessary personal details.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Storage and retention","url":"privacidade.html#storage-and-retention","text":"Storage and retention\r\nPreferences and images generally reside in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CubeControl. Simulation editor data uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CubeControl-Simulation; theme, language and zoom remain shared. Exported files go to your chosen location.\r\n\r\nThe playlist references files without copying them; order and paths are stored in backing-playlist-v1.json, while playback settings remain in memory for this session. REC recordings reside in Recordings under the active data directory, separate in simulation; the old backing-tracks-v1.json is neither loaded nor updated. Images reside in Images, with associations in gear-images-v1.json. Metronome preferences, manual BPM and per-file beat alignment reside in backing-metronome-v1.json; imported sounds are copied to metronome-sounds. The download folder and video IDs mapped to completed files reside in youtube-downloads-v1.json (also stores the preview-on-hover preference). Automatic bank, IR, amp and effect recovery snapshots remain in memory for the current session; the editor does not generate or reload pending preview files after restart. Explicitly exported backups and adjustments remain in your chosen location. See Backups and recovery. Local files remain until replaced or deleted; backups have no general automatic expiry. Uninstalling the executable does not remove this data. Pedal settings remain independently on the device. See Recovery.\r\n\r\nPersonal packs are stored in IrPacks, WAVs imported from portable packs in ImportedIrs, and custom names in ir-pack-names-v1.json, under the editor data directory. Importing can copy WAVs before the draft is saved; discarding the draft does not delete those copies.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"External services","url":"privacidade.html#external-services","text":"External services\r\nThe app does not automatically send your presets, files, device information or diagnostics to its developer or the pedal manufacturer, or sell them for advertising. YouTube search, download and audio preview, including previews triggered by hovering over a result, uses internet tools to contact external services; queries and media requests are subject to those services' policies. Local playback and documentation do not require these requests.\r\n\r\nVoluntary sharing through email or another service occurs outside local editing. Review content and the receiving service's terms. Windows, synchronization, backup and distribution services may process data under their own policies.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Control and deletion","url":"privacidade.html#control-and-deletion","text":"Control and deletion\r\nYou can change preferences, disconnect the pedal and delete local/exported files with Windows. Before deleting the data folder, finish or restore previews, close the app and preserve needed backups. Defaults may be recreated next time. Removing a track from the list does not delete its audio; exporting creates a separate file. Computer deletion does not erase pedal settings, exported copies or external backups.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Security","url":"privacidade.html#security","text":"Security\r\nLocal storage reduces transmission requirements. Access depends on Windows permissions and computer security; the app does not guarantee its own file encryption. Keep Windows updated, protect your account and control access to backups. No storage method provides absolute protection against loss or unauthorized access.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Rights and contact","url":"privacidade.html#rights-and-contact","text":"Rights and contact\r\nWhere the controller processes personal data, applicable rights under Brazil's LGPD include confirmation/access, correction, sharing information and, where legally applicable, anonymization, blocking, deletion, portability and withdrawal of consent. You may petition ANPD. Use the contact above for requests. The controller has no remote access to files held exclusively on your computer; manage those locally.\r\n\r\nIf support requires sending personal information, its purpose, legal basis, recipients and retention period or criteria must be explained for that support request. App use does not grant generic consent for additional purposes. Legal reference: Brazilian Law 13,709/2018.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Privacy","section":"Changes","url":"privacidade.html#changes","text":"Changes\r\nThis policy may be updated when features or processing practices change. Its revision date will be displayed. New collection or transmission conditions must be disclosed before processing, with consent where legally required.","keywords":"privacidade privacy dados data LGPD YouTube"},{"title":"Terms along the way","section":"Terms along the way","url":"index.html#glossary","text":"Preset A set of tone settings. A/B/C identifies three editing and saving destinations. IR — impulse response A file describing a response used by the cabinet section. An IR WAV is not a song. RAM Memory used while the device operates. A RAM preview does not automatically replace a saved slot. Flash Persistent device memory. Writing a slot replaces its content. USB-MIDI The message channel between editor and pedal. Audio playback uses Windows audio devices. dBFS A digital audio level scale. 0 dBFS is the reference ceiling; gain in dB is a different control.","keywords":""},{"title":"Three destinations for an edit","section":"Three destinations for an edit","url":"index.html#edit-paths","text":"Hearing a change, saving a file and writing to the pedal are different actions. Conceptual diagram. Available actions depend on the feature; chorus, phaser, delay and reverb creators do not write their settings to permanent memory.","keywords":""}],"empty":"No results. Try another term.","results":"results"};
